# Where the app looks for the API.
#
# Build-time, not runtime: Vite inlines it, so changing it means a redeploy.
# Left unset the client falls back to the deployed Worker, which is what a
# production Pages build wants — this file is here for pointing a local dev
# server at `wrangler dev` instead.
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
VITE_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8787

# Basemap imagery. Optional — with no key the map draws its own basemap and
# everything else works unchanged, which is why this is not required to run the
# app. Get a free key at maptiler.com (no card needed) and drop it here.
#
# Build-time, like VITE_API_URL: for the deployed site set it as an environment
# variable on the Cloudflare Pages project, not in this file.
VITE_MAPTILER_KEY=

# The Google Maps basemap. Optional, and all-or-nothing: both values are needed
# or the app keeps its own renderer.
#
# The key is the referrer-restricted *browser* key — not the Worker's geocoding
# key. Vite inlines it into the bundle, so it is public by design; the website
# restrictions on the key and its narrow API list are what protect it, not
# secrecy. Restrict it to Maps JavaScript API, Places API (New) and Street View
# Static API, and nothing else.
VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_KEY=

# A Map ID from Google Cloud console -> Google Maps Platform -> Map Management.
#
# Required, not optional. Advanced markers do not render without one, and they
# are how this app's own pin design survives the move to Google — they are real
# DOM rather than a sprite sheet. A key with no Map ID gives you a basemap with
# no leads on it, which is worse than no Google map at all, so the app treats
# that as unconfigured and says so.
VITE_GOOGLE_MAP_ID=
